- Text arguments must be strings. Non-string throws `TypeError` whose message starts with the function name and a colon. Out-of-range numeric args throw `RangeError` with the same prefix. Tests assert error class and message prefix, never full message text.
- No state: no argument mutation, no caching, no environment reads. Same args → equal values.
- One commit per task, `feat:` prefix, imperative, test file and implementation in the same commit. Never commit while `npm test` is red.
- English prose only; RTL, no-space scripts, and markup stripping are out of scope.
- `tokenize` is the single private definition of "word"; wordCount, topWords, readingTimeMinutes build on it. Each task only appends a function and widens the export line; no rewrites of earlier tasks' code or tests.
